  "decision_conditions": [
    "Before the development hereby permitted is commenced, a scheme for protecting the proposed dwellings from noise shall be submitted and approved by the Local Planning Authority to ensure that the noise level of 35 dBLAeq,16 hour in living rooms and bedrooms during the daytime (0700 to 2300 hours) and 30 dBLAeq,8 hour  and 45 dBLAFmax during the night time (2300 to 0700 hours) in bedrooms in accordance with BS8233:2014. Where these levels cannot be met with windows open appropriate acoustic ventilation should be provided so that the room can be sufficiently ventilated.  The acoustic performance of any passive vent, variable speed mechanical air supply unit or whole house ventilation must be sufficient to ensure that the noise level standards given above are not compromised.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the future occupants and neighbours by minimising impacts of the development that would otherwise give rise to nuisance in accordance with policies 9 and 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
